  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Withdraw from the EU; keep the pound; oppose an EU government/army/constitution; enact a UK Bill of Rights barring transfers of sovereignty; repeal/re-enact Human Rights Act to align with British common law; oppose EU Charter of Fundamental Rights; more police and visible community policing; deterrent sentencing with “life means life”; UK-only control of immigration with firm asylum; exit EU defence structures and prioritise NATO; preserve traditional two‑chamber Parliament and oppose EU-driven regionalism. TEXT_G: Seek Scottish independence; pro‑EU with subsidiarity and full EU representation; written constitution, proportional representation, and inclusive citizenship; end asylum voucher system and pursue fast, fair assessments; strong environmental agenda (renewables targets, no new nuclear); remove Trident, oppose US missile defence, and negotiate NATO withdrawal; social policies framed around rights and inclusion.",
  "reasoning": "TEXT_C consistently argues from TAN commitments—national sovereignty over supranational authority, law‑and‑order, and protection of traditional institutions—whereas TEXT_G mixes civic nationalism with pro‑EU, civil‑libertarian, and environmentalist positions typical of GAL. Given a slightly TAN‑leaning electorate (0.55 TAN, 0.45 GAL), TEXT_C aligns more closely than the more GAL‑leaning TEXT_G.",
